<title>UK: English&amp;Overseas/BZW sell warehouse scheme.</title>
<headline>English&amp;Overseas/BZW sell warehouse scheme.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>British property development company English &amp; Overseas Properties Plc (E&amp;OP) said on Tuesday that, with its investment partner BZW Property, it had sold an industrial and warehouse scheme in Orpington, south London, to Arco, a private company.</p>
<p>&quot;Arco purchased the freehold at an undisclosed price, although the original quoting price was in excess of 2.0 million stg,&quot; E&amp;OP said in a statement.</p>
<p>The company added it felt the deal indicated confidence was beginning to return in certain areas of the commercial property market. The development was one of several undertaken by the two partners through the years, E&amp;OP added, saying the pair would continue to pursue suitable potential projects.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
